        "# Global state\n",
        "\n",
        "Global state is state shared across a process or interpreter rather than confined to a local operation. Changes to shared state can affect other code and may need synchronization.\n",
        "\n",
        "Source: [Python glossary](https://docs.python.org/3/glossary.html#term-global-state)"
      ]
    }
